## Solution 3: Tune `max_concurrent_requests` Aggressively

If you must use `s3 sync`, the default `10` concurrent requests is the problem:

```ini
# ~/.aws/config
[default]
s3 =
    max_concurrent_requests = 1000   # was 10 by default!
    max_queue_size = 100000
    multipart_threshold = 128MB      # don't multipart small files
    multipart_chunksize = 128MB
```

```ksh
# Also override per-command:
AWS_MAX_CONCURRENT_REQUESTS=1000 aws s3 sync ./folder s3://bucket/folder/
```

